This is a tutorial of Ariadne CDCL, written as a simple self-contained example (SSCE).
It is intentionally built as a standalone project and assumes that the ariadne-cdcl library has already been installed.

To compile and run the tutorial:

1. mkdir build
2. cd build
3. cmake ..
4. cmake --build .
5. ./tutorial_cdcl

If Ariadne CDCL was installed to a non-standard prefix, pass it when configuring:

    cmake .. -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=/path/to/ariadne-cdcl/install

On Windows with Ninja:

    cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=C:/path/to/install
    cmake --build build
    .\build\tutorial_cdcl.exe
